            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="MER04" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Georges Nicholas</forename>
                        <surname>Mergez</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1772-01-04">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1846-11-25"/>
                    <occupation>General</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> A General in the Naploeonic Army who married Hocroft's daughter by his second marriage
    <persName key="HOL10">Sophie Cole (nee Holcroft)</persName>. He was created a Baron in 1809.  The couple lived abroad for much of the time.
    Mergez, who was Danton's cousin, was in London in 1792-3 with Recordain (possibly recorded at Recordat by Godwin - see Hampson p. 79), another relation of Danton's. 
    He appears as Merget in Godwin's diary in these earlier years.
  </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">Norman Hampson,<title> Danton</title>, London, 1978</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
